Z||000000||pherder||03-06-2000||07:22 PM||||In the mail today, I received my splash shields from Rodney Dickman.  I opened the Priority Mail package and unpacked the two sets that I ordered.<P>I can't believe I could get so excited over two pair of rubber mats!<P>Rodney has done it again!  They look beautiful!  Compared to the 12 year old set that was falling off my Fieros, well, there isn't a comparison!  Better than new!  Too bad they get put where you can't hardly see them.<P>Paul (AGAIN, a happy Rodney Dickman customer!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>||||reg||14
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||03-07-2000||09:35 PM||||I just put in Rodney's competition shifter and shifter arm last weekend, big big improvement over the stock shifter.  I'm happy with his stuff too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bruce||03-07-2000||09:52 PM||||I've only purchased a couple of decals from Rodney, but even those were done with great care. We're pretty lucky to have some really good suppliers associated with this forum!<BR>bb||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-07-2000||11:15 PM||||To get the clutch working again on my 85 GT after I replaced the aluminum pedal with a steel one. I had two options: 1) buy a new clutch master cylinder that would fit the new pedal and then have to bleed the blasted clutch hydraulic system or 2) have Rodney send me a custom made bushing for $4.50, including shipping, that slips on and fixes your problem with no hassles. Thanks Rodney!||||reg||1
Z||000004||88 Database Nut||03-08-2000||07:18 AM||||I too got the splash shields for my 88GT, and<BR>they are the perfect replacement for the tattered and torn old one and the missing other one!  Way to go Rodney, another example of Rodney stepping in and taking the financial risk to manufacture quality replacement parts for our cars.  It might be a couple of years until he recoups his investment on these shields, but that didn't stop him.  These are just what I needed to keep the road dirt off my newly cleaned engine and tranny.  Thanks Rodney!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
